# Edits inside chemfiles' tng.tar.gz, applied by
# chemfiles-0.10.4-external-sources.sh before chemfiles unpacks the archive.
#
# Hostile files, tng/src/lib/tng_io.c:
#   Block headers and contents must fit in the file, and the block name
#   read is checked. tng_freadstr terminates what it reads.
#   The molecules block bounds every count by the block size, allocates
#   zeroed arrays before it stores the counts, checks the molecule count
#   product, requires chains, residues and atoms to add up, and checks
#   every read. A block that fails leaves no molecules behind, since the
#   callers go on after a failed block.
#   Data blocks check their counts, strides, particle range and lengths
#   against the block, refuse codecs this build cannot decode, and copy
#   or byte-swap only the values read. gzip data must inflate to the
#   recorded size, which deflate's 1032:1 limit bounds before anything is
#   allocated, and a string block must hold a byte for each string.
#   String data is allocated and freed with the sizes it was allocated
#   with; the destructors used the counts of the last block read.
#   Particle mapping blocks check their range against the block and the
#   frame set, and each real particle number against the particle count.
#   Values are allocated zeroed, and reading the values of a frame set
#   whose blocks left a particle without values is an error instead of
#   returning uninitialised memory (a 2.5 kB file declared 100663311
#   particles and stored positions for 15).
#   tng_uncompress passes compressed and uncompressed byte lengths into
#   tng_compress_uncompress[_float]_bounded and Ptngc_unpack_array_bounded;
#   unpack_array_triplet and unpack_array_stop_bits check ptr < end before
#   every byte read and bound coding parameters and bit counts.
#   tng_util_trajectory_open closes the handle on failure instead of
#   leaking it.
